In article <1991Feb27.011241.15552@usenet.ins.cwru.edu> wooledge@skybridge.SCL.CWRU.Edu (Gregory Wooledge) writes:
>In article <627@ssp9.idca.tds.philips.nl> dolf@idca.tds.philips.nl (Dolf Grunbauer) writes:
>>I agree with this one. I don't think there is a difference between right-
>>or left ring finger, so there is no real point in asking. Maybe another
>>NETHACKOPTION should be defined to select the preferred first ring-finger.
>Ever had a cursed weapon?  Try to remove your right-hand ring while wielding
>one of them....

Well, I tend to not wield just any weapon I find, so wielding a cursed weapon
is very rare to me, but you (and some others) are right. I tested in debug mode
and it seems that using the right ring finger is impossible when wielding a
cursed weapon. Now the next question is: why should one be asked on which ring
finger the ring is to be worn when the right ring finger is impossible ??
When I already have one ring on then the next ring automatically (i.e. without
asking) put on the other finger.

Another interresting question is: when wearing a cursed shield it is still
possible to put on a ring on both the left and right hand. Is this correct ?
I would assume that in this case the left ring finger should not be usable.
(BTW: I tested this in debug mode on NH3.0 PL9 (not 10)).
